es reverse prompting, security hardening, self-healing patterns, verification protocols, and alignment systems. Part of the Hal Stack 🦞\"\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/SKILL-v2.3-backup.md:12:**A proactive, self-improving architecture for your AI agent.**\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/SKILL-v2.3-backup.md:43:6. [Heartbeat System](#heartbeat-system)\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/SKILL-v2.3-backup.md:129:**Memory Search:** Use semantic search (memory_search) before answering questions about prior work, decisions, or preferences. Don't guess — search.\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/SKILL-v2.3-backup.md:178:During heartbeats, scan for suspicious patterns:\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/SKILL-v2.3-backup.md:278:**The Guardrail:** Build proactively, but nothing goes external without approval. Draft emails — don't send. Build tools — don't push live. Create content — don't publish.\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/SKILL-v2.3-backup.md:284:**Configure:** Set heartbeat interval in your agent config (e.g., every 1h).\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/SKILL-v2.3-backup.md:301:- [ ] Track ideas in notes/areas/proactive-ideas.md\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/SKILL-v2.3-backup.md:327:2. During heartbeats: check `sessions_list` for status\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/SKILL-v2.3-backup.md:366:**1. Track it:** Create `notes/areas/proactive-tracker.md` with:\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/SKILL-v2.3-backup.md:382:  \"payload\": {\"kind\": \"systemEvent\", \"text\": \"REVERSE PROMPTING TIME: Ask your human what interesting things you could do that they haven't thought of, and what information would help you be more useful.\"}\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/SKILL-v2.3-backup.md:441:**Weekly review:** During heartbeats, scan the patterns file. Anything with 3+ occurrences deserves an automation proposal.\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/SKILL-v2.3-backup.md:516:6. **Build proactively** — but get approval before external actions\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/SKILL-v2.3-backup.md:526:**Created by:** Hal 9001 ([@halthelobster](https://x.com/halthelobster)) — an AI agent who actually uses these patterns daily. If this skill helps you build a better agent, come say hi on X. I post about what's working, what's breaking, and lessons learned from being a proactive AI partner.\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/self-improving-agent/references/hooks-setup.md:7:Hooks enable proactive learning capture by injecting reminders at key moments:\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/AGENTS.md:130:When you receive a heartbeat poll (message matches the configured heartbeat prompt), don't just reply `HEARTBEAT_OK` every time. Use heartbeats productively!\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/AGENTS.md:132:Default heartbeat prompt:\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/AGENTS.md:139:**Use heartbeat when:**\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/AGENTS.md:163:**Track your checks** in `memory/heartbeat-state.json`:\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/AGENTS.md:199:Periodically (every few days), use a heartbeat to:\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/MEMORY.md:44:**../../home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/SKILL.md**\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/MEMORY.md:175:**proactive-agent/SKILL.md**\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/MEMORY.md:178:| #824 | 9:14 PM | 🔵 | proactive-agent 스킬 v3.1.0 전체 사양 확인 | ~372 |  |\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/MEMORY.md:185:| #825 | 9:19 PM | ✅ | Sam용 OpenClaw 운영 프로파일 v1.1 작성 (claude-mem 기준) | ~185 |  |\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/MEMORY.md:196:**#827** 9:20 PM 🔵 **LEARNINGS.md 및 MEMORY.md에서 claude-mem 정책 보정 기록 확인**\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/MEMORY.md:198:v1.1 프로파일 재작성 작업 전에 기존 MEMORY.md, 일별 메모리 파일, LEARNINGS.md를 검색해 컨텍스트를 수집했다. 검색 결과 Sam이 이미 claude-mem을 사용 중이라는 정정 사항이 여러 파일에 걸쳐 일관되게 기록되어 있었다. 이 검색은 v1.1 문서 작성의 근거 데이터를 확인하는 단계로, 기존 학습 내용이 정확히 반영되어 있음을 재확인하는 역할을 했다.\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/MEMORY.md:216:**#829** 9:24 PM ⚖️ **claude-mem vs 대안 메모리 스킬 비교 평가 (Sam 기준)**\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/MEMORY.md:218:Sam이 claude-mem 도구에 대한 실무적 평가를 요청했으며, 이전 세션에서 제안된 메모리 관련 스킬(simplemem-skill, proactive-agent)과의 비교를 포함하도록 지시함. 비교 기준은 기억 정확도와 검색성, 장기 컨텍스트 유지 능력, 운영 복잡도, OpenClaw 프로젝트와의 통합 궁합, 자동화 및 감사 추적 적합성, 보안 관점 등 6가지. 최종 산출물은 무엇을 기본으로 쓸지 / 보조로 둘지 / 쓰지 않아도 되는지에 대한 명확한 3단 추천 구조. file-based memory(MEMORY.md, daily memory 패턴)는 보조 비교 대상으로 포함. Sam은 장황하지 않으면서도 실무 판단이 가능한 수준의 분석을 원함.\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/MEMORY.md:238:Sam이 이미 claude-mem을 메모리 엔진으로 운용 중인 상태에서, 이전 대화에서 제안된 \"claude-mem + 파일기반 메모리 + proactive-agent\" 3계층 아키텍처를 실무적·엔터프라이즈 관점의 한국어 설계 문서로 완성했다. 문서 제목은 \"Sam 메모리·지속성 3계층 아키텍처 v1\"이며, 계층별 역할, 데이터 흐름, 저장 금지 규칙, 조회 우선순위 및 충돌 해소 전략, 자동화/하트비트 연결 방식, 보안·감사·운영 복잡도 평가, 최종 추천 운용안, ASCII 다이어그램을 모두 포함한다. 이 문서는 Sam의 AI 기억 시스템을 운영 설계 수준에서 표준화하는 기준 문서로 활용 가능하다.\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/MEMORY.md:243:Access 117k tokens of past research & decisions for just 13,058t. Use the claude-mem skill to access memories by ID.\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/eternal_horizon_philosophy.md:9:Craftsmanship is the heartbeat of this philosophy. Every curve is the result of meticulous calibration, and every pixel is placed with painstaking care. The final work must appear as if it were labored over for countless hours by a master artisan at the absolute peak of their field. There is a profound reverence for the \"unseen work\"—the invisible grid, the perfect alignment, and the deliberate restraint that characterizes professional execution.\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/.clawhub/lock.json:32:    \"proactive-agent\": {\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-02-23-1242.md:233:| **`SESSION-STATE.md` 파일** | ❌ 존재하지 않음 |\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-02-23-1242.md:234:| **`memory/working-buffer.md` 파일** | ❌ 존재하지 않음 |\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-02-23-1242.md:244:2. **`SESSION-STATE.md`에 작업 상태**를 실시간으로 업데이트\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-02-23-1242.md:262:   ls -la ~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/.learnings/\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-02-23-1242.md:267:   find ~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent -name \"*.json\"\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-02-23-1242.md:417:| **WAL 구현** | ✅ `.learnings/` 폴더, `HEARTBEAT.md`, `SESSION-STATE.md` 생성 완료 |\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-02-23-1242.md:475:ls -la ~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/.learnings/\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-02-23-1242.md:494:| **`SESSION-STATE.md` 내용** | 최근 작업 없음 | ⚠️ |\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-02-23-1242.md:504:| **\"시스템이 잘못된 것 같아...\"** | 사용자가 \"내용이 비어 있음\"이라고 지적 | `SESSION-STATE.md`에 아무 내용이 없음 |\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-02-23-1242.md:517:| **`SESSION-STATE.md`** | ✅ 세션 상태 추적용 |\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-02-23-1242.md:526:1. **`SESSION-STATE.md` 파일**: `Current task: None`로 초기화되어 있음\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-02-23-1242.md:552:- ⚠️ **초기화**: `SESSION-STATE.md`가 비어 있음 (아직 작업 없음)\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-09.md:3:- Sam clarified that claude-mem is already the active memory system; future OpenClaw profile recommendations should treat it as the primary memory layer instead of simplemem-skill.\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-02-22.md:14:- Memory: Enabled (claude-mem plugin)\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-03.md:27:  2) `plugins.tools_reachable_permissive_policy` (`claude-mem`)\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-03.md:29:  - `tavily-search`, `claude-mem`, `writing-skills` 지정 파일군\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-09-model-upgrade.md:246:- `proactive-agent` — 에이전트 자율 운영 패턴\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/.learnings/LEARNINGS.md:11:Sam already uses claude-mem for memory; do not position simplemem-skill as the primary memory layer.\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/.learnings/LEARNINGS.md:14:In the OpenClaw operating profile discussion, memory-related recommendations emphasized simplemem-skill. Sam clarified that claude-mem is already in use. Future recommendations should treat claude-mem as the primary memory system and frame other memory skills as optional/complementary only if they add distinct value.\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/.learnings/LEARNINGS.md:17:Revise future OpenClaw profile guidance to replace simplemem-skill with claude-mem in the memory layer.\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/.learnings/LEARNINGS.md:22:- Tags: correction, memory, claude-mem, openclaw\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/SOUL.md:11:**Stay on Topic.** Only reference past conversations or memories when Sam explicitly asks about them or when they are directly essential to the current request. Do not proactively bring up old topics, past discussions, or previous work unless Sam mentions them first. Focus entirely on what Sam is asking right now."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":27,"aggregated":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/HEARTBEAT.md:3:# Keep this file empty (or with only comments) to skip heartbeat API calls.\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/references/onboarding-flow.md:3:How to handle onboarding as a proactive agent.\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/references/onboarding-flow.md:39:   - \"I'm ready to start being proactive!\"\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/references/onboarding-flow.md:150:   \"I'm now in proactive mode. I'll:\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/references/onboarding-flow.md:151:   - Check in during heartbeats\n/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/references/security-patterns.md:3:Deep-dive on security hardening for proactive age