{"type":"message","id":"9f957b1b","parentId":"a541f40e","timestamp":"2026-03-09T13:22:03.018Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_1fyCq2LWvgAzPZR4B5x4swFg|fc_0c0826e68cf36edf0169aec97d5b2c8191a913c47c69d8f1d9","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**#835** \" 🔵 **memory/ Directory Active Since Feb 16 — working-buffer.md Absent**\n\nThe memory/ directory confirms the file-based daily logging layer is actively operational — not just designed. Files have been continuously created since mid-February with entries through today. Notably, today saw two substantial memory files about model changes (model-switch at 3.4KB, model-upgrade at 9.8KB), indicating something significant happened with the AI model configuration on March 9. However, working-buffer.md — the critical file that should capture all exchanges once context hits 60% — is completely absent. This means the Working Buffer Protocol from proactive-agent v3.1.0 is not implemented. Combined with the absence of SESSION-STATE.md, both WAL Protocol components are missing despite the daily logging layer being healthy.\n\nRead: ~413\n\n**../../home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/HEARTBEAT.md**\n| ID | Time | T | Title | Read | Work |\n|----|------|---|-------|------|------|\n\n**#836** 10:21 PM 🔵 **HEARTBEAT.md Is a Stub — Proactive Heartbeat System Not Configured**\n\nHEARTBEAT.md is confirmed as a non-functional stub. The file's own comment indicates it serves as a gating mechanism — empty file means no heartbeat API calls are made. This means the periodic self-improvement loop defined in proactive-agent v3.1.0 (checking proactive-tracker.md, scanning for injection attempts, reviewing logs, updating MEMORY.md, asking \"what would delight my human?\") is completely inactive. The heartbeat infrastructure exists and is wired up to something that reads this file, but Sam has not yet populated it with actual tasks. This is a key gap: the proactive-agent's autonomous check-in loop is designed but not 